# Everything has an owner so that no pull request sits with nobody named on it.
# The interesting entries are the ones below the catch all, where a change is
# cheap to make and expensive to get wrong.

*                       @tamnd

# The pin and the drift watcher decide what every citation in the book means.
# Moving either of them silently invalidates work that is already merged.
/refcheck.toml          @tamnd
/drift.toml             @tamnd

# The claim ledger is the record of what this book says is true and how it was
# checked. An edit here is a claim about the VM, not a docs change.
/blueprints/ledger.toml @tamnd

# The checkers are the only thing standing between the house style and the
# gradual return of the word obviously.
/tools/                 @tamnd
/.github/workflows/     @tamnd
